The cases.json in this directory is copied verbatim from plannotator/sem-jiff
(https://github.com/plannotator/sem-jiff), used here as an external conformance suite for our
own engine. It is not modified.

all-cases.json merges sem-jiff's suites verbatim (stress 163, traps 129, trials 69, symbols 56,
labels 27 = 444), tagging each case with the directory it came from as `area`. Nothing inside a
case is edited. Only the 229 cases that carry a machine-checkable `ops`/`expect` list can be scored;
the rest express their expectation in prose and are kept for manual and model review.

all-cases.json carries only the 229 cases that state their expectation as a list of operation
types. The remaining 215 express it in prose or a status word ("clears"), which no engine can be
scored against; they were removed rather than scored, because a case that cannot fail is not
evidence.
